# Opens a PDF and a Markdown file from the demo Files place and asserts what is on the page, by test id. One `step` per line, as in scripts/proof-lane5.sh:
# `expect <id>` means the tree has a view with that testId; `absent <id>` means it has none. Run in demo mode (the Files place is the demo computer). The tray is the bar-mark (the tetramark) and its glyph buttons: place-<slug>.
# What only a device or simulator can prove: that WKWebView draws the PDF in the iframe from the `app:/cache/files/...` scheme (doc-frame has a size and
# the shot is not blank), that the Reader slot and the deck show ONE slot for the file, and the console lines named below.
tap bar-mark
clock +600 real
tap place-files
clock +1200 real
tap "files-row-/Documents"
clock +800 real
# PDF: the Reader document opens in one slot, the frame draws, and no placeholder is left.
tap "files-row-/Documents/Council minutes.pdf"
clock +2500 real
clock data
tree
expect doc-pages
expect doc-frame
absent doc-loading
absent doc-missing
shot files-open-pdf
# The deck lists the file once (a DOCUMENT slot and no FILE slot for it).
tap bar-mark
clock +600 real
tree
absent "launcher-open-file:/Documents/Council minutes.pdf"
shot files-open-pdf-deck
# Opening it again goes to the same slot (the tray is still open from the deck check).
tap place-files
clock +800 real
tap "files-row-/Documents/Council minutes.pdf"
clock +1500 real
tree
expect doc-pages
shot files-open-pdf-again
# Markdown: a Texture document with its text.
tap bar-mark
clock +600 real
tap place-files
clock +800 real
tap "files-row-/Documents/Harbor notes.md"
clock +1500 real
clock data
tree
expect reader-dek
absent reader-empty
shot files-open-markdown
# Console, from the device log: AUTORADIO file open kind=pdf bytes=<n> from=<network|cache> ms=<n> ok=true why=-
#                               AUTORADIO file page kind=pdf sections=<n> frame=pdf      (frame=text means the original could not be shown: a bug to report)
#                               AUTORADIO file open kind=md bytes=<n> from=<store|cache|network> ms=<n> ok=true why=-
